// Awaitable — the consumption side of the async model (ASYNC_PLAN.md,
// "Awaitable trait"). Park-flavored by design: `wait` MAY park the current
// execution context (inside a fiber it parks the fiber and frees its
// worker; on a raw thread it blocks). A Rust-style poll/Waker trait is
// deliberately rejected — it would smuggle the state-machine transform back
// in through the trait definition.
//
// `Task<T>` is the conformer: `Thread(...).start()` and `Fiber(...).start()`
// both yield one, so a generic helper taking `Awaitable` waits on either.
// The trait is deliberately NOT the place for must-start semantics —
// start-optional lifecycles are legitimate for user primitives; must-start
// is a per-struct `#destroy` contract (see Thread.nm / Fiber.nm and
// ASYNC_PLAN_2.md).

/**
 * Something whose completion can be waited on (may park the current context)
 **/
pub trait Awaitable {
	func wait = (ref self) {
	}
}
